--[[
    ⚔️ Anime Adventures — Smart Farm v1.5  (NexusLib)

    One script for the lobby and every match place:
      • Lobby:  free rewards → spends with floors (gold shop Star Fruits, optional summons) → rank every
                mode in gems per minute → join a pad, lock the level, start
      • Match:  place each unit where enemies spend the most time in range, layering further down the road
                when enemies get past (a leak gets a unit in its way), buy the best damage per yen — or the
                farm unit while it still pays back and the defense holds — fire abilities, then replay /
                next act / back to the lobby by the same ranking
      • Simulator: plays each mode with your team first (the game's own HP, waves, wave pay and skip timing),
                calibrated by every real run; its odds go into the ranking and the team / evolution planner
      • Path:   evolution goals and their items, smart evolve, and takedown training (a unit whose evolution
                needs its own takedowns joins runs the simulator says you still win with 30% tougher enemies)

    Every number comes from the game's own modules (Units, Waves, Levels, Attacks, Traits, UnitServiceCore
    formulas, the live unit stats that already include level, traits, stat rolls, curses and relics) and
    is corrected by what really happened (run times, wins, refused spots, measured damage per unit). Units the
    game ships without their upgrades are learned in matches and count as "strength unknown" until then.
    Community knowledge (C.TIERS): tier ratings, banner picks, buff chaining (tested before use), unit
    tips and promo codes.
    Settings: AA_SmartFarm/settings.json · learning: AA_SmartFarm/brain.json · log: AA_SmartFarm/log.txt
]]

-- claim the "running" slot synchronously, before any yield, so two queued loaders can't both start
if _G.AA_SF and _G.AA_SF.alive then return end
local VERSION = "1.7"
-- what changed, newest first (Updates tab; a one-time notice when a player first runs a new version)
local CHANGELOG = {
    { v = "1.0", date = "Oct 30, 2026", title = "First version", items = {
        { "🗺️", "Picks the best mode", "Daily Challenge, the half-hour Challenge, first clears (Normal and Hard), raids, Fool's Hunt and farming, ranked by gems per minute from the game's own rewards and your real run times.", "NEW" },
        { "💰", "Farm unit or damage?", "Buys the farm unit and its upgrades only while they pay back before the match ends and enemies die early on the road; otherwise it buys damage.", "NEW" },
        { "⭐", "Traits, relics and elements", "Unit strength comes from the game's formula at full upgrade: level, trait (Unique, Golden...), stat rolls, curses, relic buffs and the mode's weak/strong elements.", "NEW" },
        { "📍", "Smart placement", "Each unit goes where it covers the most road. Spots the server refuses are remembered per map.", "NEW" },
        { "🛡️", "Defense in depth", "Tracks how far down the road your units reach. When enemies get to the end of that stretch, the next unit goes further down the road. If one slips past them all, a unit goes right in its way: one enemy at your base ends the run.", "NEW" },
        { "🎁", "Free rewards", "Daily login, finished quests, battle pass and first-clear milestones are claimed for you.", "NEW" },
        { "🧾", "Spend history", "Every gold, gem and coin spend has a floor, a stop rule and a line in the Spending tab.", "NEW" },
        { "🧪", "Battle simulator", "Plays a mode with your team before the farm spends a run on it: the game's own enemy HP, waves and yen, and the farm's own buying. It learns from every real match.", "NEW" },
        { "⏩", "Real wave timing", "The simulator plays waves the way the game does: each wave's yen ×2.6 (the world's money boost), the early skip vote (about 2 s + 2 s per enemy, at most 30 s) and an enemy at your base taking it down in seconds.", "NEW" },
        { "👥", "Best team finder", "Tries your other units against each mode's weak and strong elements and shows the team that does best (Battle tab). It only equips it if you switch that on.", "NEW" },
        { "🌟", "Evolution check", "Shows which evolutions your items already cover and what each one would change in the hardest mode you play.", "NEW" },
        { "🧬", "Smart evolve", "Evolves your best copy of a unit once it's ready and gets stronger, but only with items no bigger goal needs and only using up spare copies (never one on your team or with a trait). Every evolve shows in the log and the Spending tab. Switch it off in the Path tab.", "NEW" },
    } },
}
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, { v = "1.5", date = "Oct 30, 2026", title = "Dungeons", items = {
    { "🏰", "Dungeons", "The dungeon joins the ranking: 20 rooms in a row, one room a run. The farm goes for Rare Chests first, keeps them (and chests) for floor 20 so every luck item bought on the way counts, keeps its coins for the shops at floors 10–15, and buys chest luck in every shop (keeping coins back for it while another shop room is ahead). Rare Chests come with curses, so each curse is judged by what it does, and a curse is skipped only if the simulator says your team can't beat rooms with it. A room gives 5 tries, and clearing one refills them. Modes tab.", "NEW" },
    { "⏹️", "Infinite ends on time", "Past wave 50 an Infinite run pays only a few gems a wave. Once the daily gems are in and no unit is training there, the farm ends the run if another mode pays more a minute: it sells your units, the base falls and the run pays out as usual. Modes tab.", "NEW" },
    { "🛡️", "Fool's Hunt lessons everywhere", "Four things Fool's Hunt taught now work with your own team too (dungeons, challenges, story, raids): on the last wave each farm is sold and the yen goes into damage; once 5 units are down, at least 2 damage dealers guard the stretch before the base; once flyers show up (or a dungeon run carries the Curse of Flight), units that hit flyers get more of the yen; and short-range units get less of it, since a boss walks past them in a moment.", "IMPROVED" },
    { "🎯", "Training check", "A takedown-training check cut short by a teleport no longer counts as \"no\" for 6 hours: it's checked again.", "FIX" },
    { "⏹️", "Selling to end Infinite", "Ending an Infinite run sells every unit once and skips any the game refuses (a golden Bulby held the old loop for 14 minutes).", "FIX" },
    { "👹", "Moving up to the boss", "On the last wave with only a boss or two left, new units and upgrades go where the boss is. An attacker it has walked past is sold, and when the boss would reach your base alive (a Curse of Regen boss heals 1% of its HP a second), units waiting further down the road move up to it too, so all your damage lands together.", "NEW" },
    { "📍", "The simulator searches for spots", "At the start of a match (your own team, not Infinite or Fool's Hunt) the simulator tries spots on the map for each attacker and uses the layout that gets furthest against tough enemies. Each unit's shortlist counts the road it reaches at full range with the run's bonuses: Iron Sentinel went from reaching 72% of a road to all of it. A spot that lost on a map counts against it next time. Battle tab.", "NEW" },
    { "⏱️", "Stays for the boss", "The \"no progress for 6 minutes\" safety no longer walks out of a boss fight on the last wave (a final boss was left at half HP and the room started over).", "FIX" },
    { "👥", "Team search that counts bosses", "The team planner now also tries your damage-over-time units and every farm, and judges teams near their breaking point, where a difference shows. In a dungeon the simulator now plays each room's last-wave boss with its real HP, and damage over time stays on a lone boss instead of vanishing. With Auto-Equip Best Team on (Battle tab), the better team goes in before a dungeon run's first room and after a lost try.", "NEW" },
    { "🧪", "Simulator knows your items", "In a dungeon the simulator now counts what the run carries: damage, cooldown and range items, a damage type's bonus (Mage Coat), and the curses that make enemies tougher. It used to simulate your team as if it had bought nothing, and called rooms it then won a loss.", "FIX" },
} })
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 2, { v = "1.4", date = "Oct 30, 2026", title = "Main goal", items = {
    { "🏆", "Main goal", "Pick a unit to chase (Settings: pull goal, e.g. Chuuni, SS once evolved). The farm plays Fool's Hunt for AprilCoins while the goal needs them, pulls the April banner 10 at a time until it drops, keeps its evolve item's price, buys that item, trains its takedowns and evolves it. Path tab.", "NEW" },
    { "💱", "Live currency", "Spends read your gems and event coins the moment they change, not the profile copy that only updates after a teleport.", "FIX" },
    { "🃏", "Fool's Hunt", "Plays the team the mode deals (not yours): places each dealt card, casts Random Buff on your strongest unit, Clone and Astral Summon, picks the AprilCoin multipliers, and at 20 units sells a weak unit for a much stronger card (or discards a card that isn't worth a spot). A Refund card cashes in a farm that won't earn back its cost before the run ends, or a weak unit whose yen buys far more damage as upgrades. Extra copies of a spell card are discarded so the hand keeps room for units.", "NEW" },
    { "🔀", "Merge stacking", "Grows your strongest Fool's Hunt unit the way the guides do: a second copy goes down next to it and isn't upgraded, the first copy gets maxed, then Merge goes on the fresh copy so it keeps 1.5× the maxed one's damage and gets its own upgrades on top. Repeat for more. An Idol gets maxed early (it buffs everyone and makes upgrades cheaper).", "NEW" },
    { "📖", "Learns the mode", "Every Fool's Hunt run records the wave reached, the coins, the dealt units that carried the damage (placed first next time) and the hidden stats of every dealt unit. Path tab.", "NEW" },
} })
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 3, { v = "1.3", date = "Oct 30, 2026", title = "What the guides say", items = {
    { "📚", "Community tiers", "A community tier list (Oct 2026) now rates units the game hides: an S or SS evolution counts as joining your team, and the Path tab lists every banner unit and your own units with their ratings.", "NEW" },
    { "🎟️", "Banner picks", "The April banner only spends AprilCoins while Chuuni (SS once evolved) or Vengeful Swordsman (S) is missing, not on Violentine (B) or Kansai (D).", "IMPROVED" },
    { "🌬️", "Buff chaining", "The guides say Windsong and Commander buffs chain up to +100%. The farm tests it once in a match (a second copy's buff while one is up) and chains them from then on only if it really adds up.", "NEW" },
    { "🎯", "Unit tips", "Chuuni (Delusion) targets the strongest enemy so the boss keeps her mark; Legendary Assassin (Prime) targets the closest and stands near the exit.", "NEW" },
    { "🎁", "Codes", "Redeems the promo codes from the guides in the lobby, each one your account hasn't used.", "NEW" },
} })
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 4, { v = "1.2", date = "Oct 30, 2026", title = "Hidden unit stats", items = {
    { "🔍", "Hidden unit stats", "The game hides the upgrades of about half its Mythic and Secret units (every April, Sakamoto and current banner unit) until they're in a match. The farm now records them when a match sends them, and until then calls those units \"strength unknown\" instead of weak: no goal value, no automatic evolve and no summons on a guess.", "FIX" },
} })
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 5, { v = "1.1", date = "Oct 30, 2026", title = "Takedown training", items = {
    { "🎯", "Takedown training", "Some evolutions need the unit's own takedowns (Shinobi (Hood) needs 7,500). The farm puts that unit on your team only for runs the simulator says you still win with 30% tougher enemies, counts its takedowns every match, and puts your team back after each run. Path tab.", "NEW" },
    { "♾️", "Infinite", "Infinite maps join the ranking: each pays gems once a day at waves 10, 25 and 50 (200 in all), and a run lasts until the base falls, so a unit in training gets far more takedowns. The first quarter of the road is kept for that unit (your other attackers stand after it), and while enemies die early the others aren't upgraded, so enemies live long enough for it to hit them. Every map sends the same number of enemies; the easy ones last longest. Modes tab.", "NEW" },
    { "📍", "Where it stands", "A takedown needs a hit before the enemy dies, so the trainee stands where enemies arrive first and goes for the newest enemy in its range, one your other units haven't killed yet.", "NEW" },
} })
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, { v = "1.7", date = "Oct 31, 2026", title = "A stronger team", items = {
    { "💪", "Team tab", "The farm now makes your 8 core units stronger with what you already have: XP food from the gold shop (gold kept for you), Stat Cubes to your grade, trait rerolls where a roll beats the trait on average, your unused relics, and a limit break once a unit is at its cap with a Divine Wish and spare units. One action at a time, each judged by how much of the team's damage it adds, with the game's own unit maths. Dry Run is on at first: it only says what it would do.", "NEW" },
    { "🎯", "Modes that make the team stronger", "The mode ranker now counts the XP a run gives your units, and values a Divine Wish, Star Remnants and Stat Cubes by what they'd do for your core units. The Daily Challenge is played once a day whatever the Farming tab says, since it pays the wish, remnants and cubes.", "NEW" },
    { "📊", "Who carries", "Each match records how much of the damage each unit dealt (Iron Sentinel's drones count as its). The Team tab weighs every change by that.", "NEW" },
    { "🎲", "Trait rolls work", "The game only rolls a trait on a unit that isn't equipped, and said so in red. The unit now leaves your team for the roll and goes back in its slot.", "FIX" },
    { "💍", "Team swaps with a Miracle Timepiece", "A team can hold one Miracle Timepiece, so a second unit carrying one was turned away, leaving an empty slot. It takes its relic off for that team now.", "FIX" },
    { "⏸️", "The Team tab finishes first", "It can only work in the lobby, and won rooms used to chain straight into the next one, so it hardly ever got a turn. The run now goes through the lobby whenever the Team tab has something to do, and it finishes before the next room. Going through the lobby doesn't cost a choice of room.", "NEW" },
    { "🔮", "Smart Relics", "Before a run, your relics move to where they add the most damage on the team that's playing, counting what each copy really rolled: its damage types, the Timepiece's extra hit on slow attackers, crit, flyers. Once a team has them, they only move again for +2% or more. Team tab.", "NEW" },
    { "🔥", "Two fuses", "The game has two, so the Lobby tab does too. Limit Break raises the level cap. Fuse For XP feeds spare units into the one you pick, up to its level cap: only level-1 units, never locked ones, and never Mythic or better, since a limit break needs those. It stays off until you switch it on, and it can't be undone.", "NEW" },
    { "☀️", "Ready for the Summer update", "Update 21 changed how the game checks unlocked levels, which units hit flyers, and where it keeps trait odds and difficulty numbers. The farm reads all of them the new way, so it plays again and the team search and Team tab work.", "FIX" },
    { "🔁", "Replays with no teleport", "Replay and Next can now restart right where you are. The farm reloads itself on the spot, about 5 seconds, and can still change the team before the first wave. If the game teleports instead, it works as before.", "NEW" },
    { "🪽", "The new flyer rules", "Any unit can now hit flyers, for half damage and without its stun or slow unless it stands on a hill or has an anti-air attack. The simulator and the buying both play it that way.", "FIX" },
    { "🛑", "No more rerolls", "The farm no longer rerolls stats or traits, on the Team tab or the Lobby tab. Your Stat Cubes, Star Remnants and tokens stay yours to use by hand.", "IMPROVED" },
    { "🏖️", "The Summer Hunt", "The farm can now play the Summer Hunt: 50 waves, a new map and weather every hour. It picks each card by what it pays and what it costs your team, and claims finished bingo lines. It never spends Summer Pearls or trades gems for them. Turn on Summer Hunt Only to play it.", "NEW" },
    { "🧪", "A tougher team test", "The team search used to stop testing at enemies ×4, so on easy maps every team looked the same and a swap could come down to seconds. It now keeps making enemies tougher until your team breaks, and a swap has to really go further over that whole test. Otherwise your team stays.", "IMPROVED" },
    { "🌀", "Windsong takes turns properly", "A second Windsong cast adds nothing while the buff is up, and doesn't renew it either, so a cast fired a moment early was wasted. Each copy now reads the buff on your units and casts only once it has really ended.", "FIX" },
    { "🔍", "Hidden units get real numbers", "The game hides many units' upgrades and attacks until they're played. The farm now fills those gaps with community data, so the team search can judge them, and the game's own numbers replace it the first time a unit plays.", "NEW" },
    { "🎯", "Banner Snipe", "Pick any unit a banner can feature. Each lobby visit reads every banner, and while one features your pick it pulls there until the unit drops, or until your gems, pearls or Legacy Gems reach the Keep line you set. Banners turn over every 4 hours: a match can't read them, but the farm knows when they've changed and stops at the lobby after the match to look. It replaces Griffin Watch (a watch that was on carries on for Griffin). Summon tab.", "NEW" },
    { "🌀", "Portal To Play", "A new pick on the Play tab. Smart plays a portal you hold when its map drops something your evolutions need, from any of the game's 38 kinds. Pick a kind to play it first whenever you hold one, or switch Portals off to keep them.", "NEW" },
    { "❄️", "Snow Reaper's Gale takes turns", "Snow Reaper (Final)'s Gale of the Moon is a switch with a bar: while it's on, enemies in her range are slowed, chilled and frozen. The farm used to flip it on and off every few seconds. Now her copies take turns: the next one goes on as the one running empties, a copy with nothing in range switches off to keep its bar, and while one copy is on a boss the others wait with theirs full.", "FIX" },
    { "📍", "Control units stand with your damage", "A unit that freezes, stuns or slows holds what's in its own range, so it now goes where your other attackers' damage reaches the road the most, and what it holds stays under all of them. Snow Reaper's copies used to go where the road was longest, sometimes 120 studs from anyone else. Control that only comes at a later upgrade counts too now: Ghost Lady (Princess) from upgrade 3, JIO from 4, Delinquent (The Universe) from 7.", "FIX" },
    { "🧠", "It learns abilities by itself", "A unit with a switch ability and a bar, like Snow Reaper's Gale, is learned the first time it shows one in a match: the upgrade it comes at, and how fast its bar fills and drains. From then on its copies take turns and it stands where your damage is. What one farm learns, every farm knows: it goes into the match records, and through the Brain Hive other players' farms know the unit before they ever play it.", "NEW" },
    { "🧊", "The simulator counts the Gale", "Snow Reaper (Final)'s Gale of the Moon now plays in the simulator: her aura on every enemy in range, the freezes and the slow, a third of the time per copy. Her attacks also read their real shapes (a circle, a cone, then the whole field) instead of one enemy, and so do Violentine's. On your Daily Challenge test it reads wave 24 and 925M where the real run went to wave 25 with 778M; before, it said wave 8 with 8M. The team search now weighs her like that.", "FIX" },
    { "✨", "A cleaner window", "Every tab is reorganized and opens with what it's for. Home is the dashboard, with a line for every part. Play holds all the choices of what to play, one control per kind (Off, On or Only this) beside its map pick, where each kind used to have two switches. Summon and Fuse replace the old Lobby tab, and fine-tuning sits under Advanced at the bottom of each tab.", "IMPROVED" },
    { "🔥", "Limit Break, your way", "On the Fuse tab: pick any unit that can still be limit broken, then tick its fodder in a table that shows each unit's rarity, level, points, evolved, trait, relic, shine and whether a goal needs it. ★ marks the farm's own safe picks, and a card shows level, Divine Wish and fodder points with a progress bar. Nothing ticked: the farm picks by its safe rule as before.", "NEW" },
    { "🐝", "Learning from other players", "Every farm that shares sends its match records to the Brain Hive, which combines them (no names or ids) and publishes the result. Your farm reads it every 6 hours and fills in what your own runs haven't measured yet: how far the simulator is off for a unit, and how many takedowns a unit in training gets on each map, so training starts on the fastest one. It also names units the simulator reads far too low. Your own runs always come first. Settings → Brain Hive.", "NEW" },
    { "📦", "Everyone inside the kill box", "In a kill box every attacker now starts on a spot that really reaches the road's last stretch. A unit that stands on hills, like Iron Sentinel, has few spots near the end, and its list used to be filled up with mid-road ones: on the Summer Hunt it stood 100 studs from the other three, reaching 30-64% of the road and none of the box. The fast start works the same way now.", "FIX" },
    { "🌐", "What one farm learns, every farm knows", "Three more things now go through the Brain Hive. Units the game ships without stats: once any farm has read one, every farm can size it, place it and put it in teams. How tough each map really is, so the simulator is right on a map before you've ever played it. And what every map and portal really drops, the hidden drops too, so the farm knows where to get an evolve item or a portal's prize. Your own runs always come first.", "NEW" },
    { "📈", "Legend Stage progress", "Legend Stage To Play now has Progress too: the next legend stage you haven't beaten, in the game's order.", "NEW" },
    { "⏩", "Auto Summon gets all its pulls", "The game refuses a pull that comes a few seconds after the last one, and the farm used to stop there for 10 minutes. It now waits a moment and carries on.", "FIX" },
    { "🔥", "Smarter Limit Break", "Fuses now use the tier list's Fusion Fodder first. They never use your best supports, control units or farm, anything rated A or higher, a unit that evolves into one of those, or your 10 strongest units.", "NEW" },
    { "🧠", "The search team comes first", "The farm looks for the best team before every run and plays whatever it ranks first. Relics now move once, after the team is settled, and a tiny relic gain no longer costs a trip to the lobby.", "FIX" },
    { "📌", "Always on top", "The window and its round button now stay above the game's own screens.", "NEW" },
    { "🧹", "Only events that are on", "The panel now shows an event's switches only while the game runs it. Fool's Hunt and the April banner are out of the game, so their switches are hidden. If they come back, their switches do too. The same goes for the Summer Hunt when it ends.", "FIX" },
    { "🔥", "Legend Stages count their weaknesses", "Enemies on Legend Stages and some raids take much more damage from certain types, up to ×3.5 for some. The team search, the simulator and the buying now all count that, so a fire and ice stage gets your fire and ice units.", "FIX" },
    { "🪼", "Elyssia (Abyssal) can be picked", "Her upgrades were hidden, so the team search skipped her. They now come from her wiki page, and the simulator plays her jellies and eels. Every unit's numbers were checked against its live page too.", "FIX" },
    { "📐", "Three ways to place your team", "Before the first wave the simulator searches the best spots on the map for three layouts and picks by how strong your team is there. Beats enemies at 1.5× strength from the road's start: a fast clear. Beats a bit more than normal strength: spread over the road. Normal strength or lower: a kill box at the road's end, now with its own best spots. It works in every mode, dungeon rooms too, except Infinite and modes that deal your team. A layout that loses steps down to a safer one on the next try, and a room's last life is always a kill box.", "NEW" },
    { "🪜", "Tougher team test in dungeons", "A dungeon team swap now has to go further up the same rising test as every other mode, up to 24× enemy strength. A tie keeps your team.", "IMPROVED" },
    { "🌬️", "Windsongs where they're needed", "A buffer now gets only the copies that keep its buff up all the time. For Windsong that's 2 for each group of attackers, taking turns, so a force at the back gets its own pair. The rest of the yen goes to your attackers.", "FIX" },
    { "🔎", "A fresh team search before every run", "Auto-Equip Best Team used to go by a saved plan, even one made hours ago with different units. Now it searches before every run with the units and levels you have right then.", "FIX" },
    { "✨", "A new look", "Fewer tabs, one home for every control, shorter descriptions and a new neon theme. Home shows what it's doing and what to play, Goals what it's working toward, Team what makes your units stronger, Lobby what you choose by hand.", "IMPROVED" },
    { "🎯", "Choose what to evolve next", "The Goals tab lists your 10 strongest evolutions, by the guides' rating and then the score at level 100. Pick one to focus on and its items and takedowns come first, or leave it on Smart Play and the farm chooses.", "NEW" },
    { "🔀", "Team swaps without the lobby", "A dungeon room that wants a different team now gets it as the room loads, before the first wave, instead of a trip to the lobby. No wave starts until all six are right, and if the swap fails the run goes to the lobby, which doesn't cost a try.", "NEW" },
    { "⏭️", "Next between story acts", "After a win the farm presses Next instead of going back to the lobby. The team is sorted out at the start of the next match, before the first wave: your training unit stays in if the simulator says the team still wins there, otherwise your own team goes back. It still stops at the lobby when the Team tab has work.", "NEW" },
    { "🗺️", "Story progress means new maps", "Farm Story Only now plays only acts you've never beaten. Hard runs of acts you've already beaten on Normal wait, and come back when the switch is off.", "FIX" },
    { "🧱", "The simulator plays stacked rooms", "In dungeon rooms your attackers stand together on the road's last stretch, and now the simulator plays them there too. It no longer calls a room lost at wave 7 when your team really gets to the boss, so its team picks and room picks go by what actually happens. Whether to take a curse is still judged the careful way.", "FIX" },
} })
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 2, { v = "1.6", date = "Oct 31, 2026", title = "A simpler window", items = {
    { "🌾", "Farming tab", "One switch to play, and five you can use to play only raids, story progress, challenges, April Coins or dungeons. All off: it plays whatever pays best.", "NEW" },
    { "🏰", "Lobby tab", "Pick a banner to summon on, a unit to fuse to, a unit and grade for its stats, and a unit to evolve (it farms the items and takedowns first). Each stays off until you switch it on.", "NEW" },
    { "⚙️", "Everything else", "The old tabs are one switch away: Settings, Show All Settings.", "IMPROVED" },
    { "👥", "Team swaps", "A swap of two units could fail without a word and leave the wrong team on. The farm now checks and tries again.", "FIX" },
    { "🧠", "A smarter simulator", "It now counts how many times an attack hits (shields lose a point per hit), plays slows and stuns on the road, and stops regen on bleeding enemies, so slow units like Mochi get the credit they earn.", "IMPROVED" },
    { "🎲", "Auto Stats waits for Worthiness", "Stat rolls are better at 100% Worthiness or more, so Auto Stats waits for it. Lobby tab, Wait For Worthiness.", "NEW" },
    { "🏰", "Best team for every dungeon room", "Before each room the farm tries your other units against that room. A new team goes on only if it holds up clearly better, and the rooms a team has really won or lost count too.", "IMPROVED" },
    { "✨", "Abilities in the simulator", "It now plays Chuuni's marks, Iron Sentinel's drones, time stops, cooldown buffs, shield breaks and built-in crits, so those units get the credit they earn when it picks teams. Summons aren't played yet.", "IMPROVED" },
    { "🩸", "Enemy abilities in the simulator", "Enemies that heal, enemies that split when they die and enemies with barriers are now played too, so it sees the rooms that are really hard.", "FIX" },
    { "🧲", "Slows get bought", "A slow or a stun now counts for what it does for your other units, not just its own damage, so Mochi goes down early. And the simulator weighs upgrades the way the farm does, so it buys in nearly the same order.", "IMPROVED" },
    { "🧿", "Curses, more carefully", "A curse lasts to room 20, and a death loses every chest in the run. Past room 10, or with chests riding on the run, a curse is taken only if the simulator says your team still beats the rooms after it; past room 15, or with many chests, it has to beat them against 30% tougher enemies. A curse the simulator can't play (Chaos, Eruption, Armor, Burst) is passed when chests are riding. Shrines follow the same rule.", "IMPROVED" },
    { "🛒", "Shop buys for your team", "Items that boost one damage type are now judged by how much of your damage is that type, not how many units are. An item that does nothing for your team isn't bought at any price.", "FIX" },
    { "🛡️", "Illusionist's base guard", "Illusionist (Final)'s ability guards the base for 10 seconds and throws back what touches it, so the farm now fires it as an enemy reaches the base. It used to fire at 90% of the road, which spent nearly all of it before the enemy arrived.", "FIX" },
} })
